{
  "id": "u04-l06b",
  "unit": "u04-food",
  "title": "Good, bad & biryani",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Three new words:\n\n- **বিরিয়ানি** (*biriyani*): biryani, the star of weddings. Old Dhaka is famous for *kachchi* biryani.\n- **খারাপ** (*kharap*) 'bad', the opposite of **ভালো**. **খারাপ না** 'not bad' is a common, modest compliment.\n- **সব** (*shob*) 'all' goes before the noun: **সব খাবার** 'all the food'. On its own it means 'everything': **আমি সব খাই** 'I eat everything'.\n\nLike ভালো, they need no verb: **ডাল খারাপ** 'the dal is bad'. Put **না** after the adjective to say 'not': **এটা খারাপ না**.",
  "vocab": [
